      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "Given that Ace and Zeppo are already in the starting lineup, we need to determine the number of ways to select the remaining 3 players from the 10 remaining players on the team.\n\nTo find this, we can use the combination formula:\n\\[\n\\binom{n}{r} = \\frac{n!}{r!(n-r)!}\n\\]\nwhere \\( n \\) is the total number of items to choose from, and \\( r \\) is the number of items to choose.\n\nHere:\n- \\( n = 10 \\) (since there are 10 players excluding Ace and Zeppo)\n- \\( r = 3 \\) (since we need to select 3 players from these 10)\n\nNow, apply the combination formula:\n\\[\n\\binom{10}{3} = \\frac{10!}{3!(10-3)!} = \\frac{10!}{3! \\cdot 7!}\n\\]\n\nWe can simplify this by canceling out the \\( 7! \\) in the numerator and the denominator:\n\\[\n\\binom{10}{3} = \\frac{10 \\times 9 \\times 8 \\times 7!}{3! \\times 7!} = \\frac{10 \\times 9 \\times 8}{3 \\times 2 \\times 1}\n\\]\n\nNext, calculate the numerator and the denominator:\n\\[\n10 \\times 9 \\times 8 = 720\n\\]\n\\[\n3 \\times 2 \\times 1 = 6\n\\]\n\nSo,\n\\[\n\\frac{720}{6} = 120\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the number of different starting lineups possible is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{120}\n\\]\n\nThe main reason why Li Yuan was able to unseat the Zhou Dynasty and establish the Sui Dynasty was ____.\nA. Better military equipment\nB. Collaboration between the ruling class and the ruled class\nC. Strong royal authority\nD. The selection system based on imperial power\nAnswer:\nD\n\nWhich of the following statements about the text is incorrect?\nA. Tightening the jaw, sticking out teeth, licking lips and making rasping sounds, are all methods used by hawks to capture food.\nB. Animals use different strategies to defend themselves against predators, such as warning strategies, deterrence strategies, defense strategies, and escape strategies.\nC. Whenever humans encounter problems, they often turn to nature, looking for inspiration from animals' survival mechanisms.\nD. To understand the evolution and origin of creatures, it is crucial to study embryology. Human embryos have just a whale's basic structure, adding five more organs, and eventually developing into the full-bodied lamb embryos. This demonstrates the theory of natural selection.\nAnswer:\nD\n\nDry ice comes in solid form, but it easily sublimates at room temperature. It's widely used for cooling and in industrial production. Which of the following is a use of dry ice?\nA. The formation of capillaries\nB. Iron smelting\nC. Preserving food\nD. Disinfection\nAnswer:\nC\n\nGelatin products, made from animal skin and bones, were used in the early days of cinema for what purpose? ____\nA. As artistic decorative elements\nB. For decorative costumes\nC. As film backing for projections\nD. As screen support materials\nAnswer:\nD\n\nThe main reason for the significant regional differences in the distribution of shipbuilding industries is ____\nA. Large market demand differences\nB. Differences in natural conditions\nC. Differences in raw material resources\nD. Differences in technology levels\nAnswer:\nA\n\nThe Shenzhou XIV spacecraft cabin uses a solid heat-resistant tile composed of high-temperature silicon oxynitride (SiON) and carbon nanotubes (CNT). Which of the following statements about this spacecraft cabin material is incorrect?\nA. High-temperature silicon oxynitride is a silvery-white solid compound.\nB. Carbon nanotubes have a high tensile strength and excellent electrical conductivity.\nC. Silicon oxynitride is composed of silicon, oxygen, and nitrogen atoms.\nD. Carbon nanotubes belong to the category of synthetic materials.\nAnswer:\nC",
