    {
      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To determine the number of different starting lineups possible for the Grunters, we need to consider the following:\n\n1. Coach Grunt needs to select 3 more players from the remaining 10 players (since Ace and Zeppo are already in the lineup).\n2. The order in which the players are selected does not matter, meaning we are looking for combinations, not permutations.\n\nThe number of ways to choose 3 players out of 10 is given by the binomial coefficient \\(\\binom{10}{3}\\). The binomial coefficient \\(\\binom{n}{k}\\) is calculated as follows:\n\n\\[\n\\binom{n}{k} = \\frac{n!}{k!(n-k)!}\n\\]\n\nIn this case, \\(n = 10\\) and \\(k = 3\\), so we have:\n\n\\[\n\\binom{10}{3} = \\frac{10!}{3!(10-3)!} = \\frac{10!}{3! \\cdot 7!}\n\\]\n\nWe can simplify this by canceling out the \\(7!\\) in the numerator and the denominator:\n\n\\[\n\\binom{10}{3} = \\frac{10 \\times 9 \\times 8 \\times 7!}{3! \\times 7!} = \\frac{10 \\times 9 \\times 8}{3!} = \\frac{10 \\times 9 \\times 8}{3 \\times 2 \\times 1} = \\frac{720}{6} = 120\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the number of different starting lineups possible is \\(\\boxed{120}\\).",
